REASON mhat: C-MHAT gives m1, m2, m3 > 0, so mhat(t) >= 1 on (0, 1/300] and B(t)/mhat(t) <= main(t)/mhat(t) + Rb(t) with Rb = R3 + R_cub + tail + far >= 0
REASON main: C-MONO gives D > 0 on [0, 1/300], so main(t)/mhat(t) is nondecreasing; its t = 1/300 value bounds every t in (0, 1/300]
REASON R3: t^3 and t^4 times untilted integrals of fixed polynomials (twlib hbar(j, a, aZ) has no t): nondecreasing in t
REASON R_cub: Q_t(t') >= Q_t(1/300) in the Loewner order for t' <= 1/300 (the t-part t cfun(a_v) of the tilt is PSD), the integrands 1, H1^4, hhat^4 are >= 0, hhat(t') <= hhat(1/300) monomialwise, and t^3 grows: nondecreasing in t
REASON tail: e^{-lam_v J a_v} decreases in J; T_v <= (1 - theta2)^{-d/2} I[1] is free of J (C-PROP, C-RANK); L2 is t, t^2 times untilted integrals: nonincreasing in J
REASON far: v1_1's PR 2J (2 far_one(a) + far_one(aZ)) majorizes the plain trace's PR (2 far_one(a) + far_one(aZ)), as 2J >= 1; C-FAR (p/J < c(a), c(aZ) for J >= 300), so J^p e^{-c J} decreases in J
REASON PR: PR = pref_arb(N), a ratio of reduced Laplacian determinants of fixed strip graphs, does not depend on J
REASON TW: every TW error sits inside the certified J = 300 enclosures; each reason compares exact J-bounds with the exact J = 300 bound, which the enclosure upper end majorizes
REASON Z4: each J-bound is twrig3's chain at its own Omega(J) and tilt T(1/J) before the comparison, so the comparison is between valid bounds, pointwise in J
CHECKS all PASS
